Z||000000||yo_sweet||12-20-2001||10:16 PM||||i have the same rims as urchin has or had on his car americanr acign mags , how will they hold up to salt if i was them daily?<P>will they be fine?<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-20-2001||11:14 PM||||My experience with mags in winter... wash or hose down frequently. Keep some kind of wax on them, or salt and sand will dull and pit them eventually. <P>If they have a clearcoat its not such a big problem, but if its chipped, the salt/dirt will seep in and tarnish. Then you'll have ugly spots.<P>Not familiar with your actual type of mags, but thats my 2 cents..<p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||12-21-2001||06:27 AM||||I used to clean, wax, spray with a coat of silicone spray on my Mercedes. Every couple of weeks or so kept em nice for me. Now I dont drive my car on salted roads, drive the others.||||reg||1
